# Adding a record to an editable grid.
#
# The row is entered in place: the framework opens it, then fills each named column. Whether it
# reaches the database follows the page's own save, the same way a value written with 'set' does.
#
# The column names come from the page file, so a typo in one of them fails during validation,
# before a browser is started.

use Supervisor
open UsrTestForm for 71d27c81-3d6b-41d9-9a39-c408c96173b6

# Creatio reopens a page on the tab it was last left on, so the tab is stated rather than assumed.
click GeneralInfoTab

# The page has a required field of its own; it has to hold something before Creatio will save.
set RichTextEditor_xnaolfg "Filled by the add-record case"

check DataGrid_0qy3003 is editable

# One column of each kind the grid offers: plain text, a checkbox, and a lookup resolved through
# its autocomplete. Not every column of an editable grid can be filled -- Creatio renders some of
# them as links or coloured labels, and those are read-only in the list whatever the grid's setting.
add-record DataGrid_0qy3003 set Full name=Multi Column Row;Address=Main street 1;Recipient's name=Mr Jon;IsEmailConfirmed=true;Job title=Developer

# Creatio swaps Close for Save/Cancel as soon as the page has unsaved changes, so neither button
# exists until a row has been added.
#
# The case cancels rather than saves, so that running the suite twice leaves the same page behind.
# Replacing this line with 'click SaveButton' is what commits the row to the database.
click CancelButton
